 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Totally understandable. Dress politely, but not too fancy, and go few minutes early so you' not rushed. That's the real worry. Walk confidently, don't lean on your napkin, and try to keep your plate balanced with your knife and fork in your right hand. Look at the menu before you go, and choose something you can explain. A meat dish is easier than a seafood one at a seafood restaurant. Ask for help, and don't be shy about that. chefs love talking food, and they' usually be happy to point you in the right direction. Only if they have one. Most modern places will just give you small dish with everything, so it' not worth it.",
